1600 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 343 0 R
/T (The Run The Rack technique is where you finish your last set, and then keep pulling out the pin and switching to the next lowest weight and you continue doing repetitions without rest, and then everytime you fatigue, you pull out the pin and go one weight lower until you reach a weight of 0. You can do this on machines by pulling out the pin and setting a lower weight each time, or on the Dumbell rack by picking up a lighter pair of dumbbells each time until you reach the lowest weight on the dumbbell rack. Use this technique on your very last set of the exercise.)
/E (The Run The Rack technique is where you finish your last set, and then keep pulling out the pin and switching to the next lowest weight and you continue doing repetitions without rest, and then everytime you fatigue, you pull out the pin and go one weight lower until you reach a weight of 0. You can do this on machines by pulling out the pin and setting a lower weight each time, or on the Dumbell rack by picking up a lighter pair of dumbbells each time until you reach the lowest weight on the dumbbell rack. Use this technique on your very last set of the exercise.)
/Pg 65 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
