<<
/Title (Slow repetitions involve controlling each phase of the movement with a tempo of 4 seconds on the lift and 4 seconds on the lowering of the weight. Think: 4 seconds up and 4 seconds down. This method increases time under tension, improves muscle control, and makes the muscle work harder during each repetition. Use this technique on every repetition this month. Slightly reduce the weight to maintain proper technique and controlled movement throughout the set.)
/Dest [40 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 5075 0 R
/First 5134 0 R
